vkd3d-shader: close HLSL front-end gaps that kept titles on Microsoft's d3dcompiler_47.

Wine's builtin d3dcompiler_47 is vkd3d-shader's HLSL compiler. Titles that compile HLSL at runtime
hand it source Microsoft's compiler accepts; each change below adds what one of them needed, in the
shape of the native behaviour:

- preproc: HLSL_VERSION is predefined (as 1) unless the caller's macros define it. Microsoft's own
  D3DX_DXGIFormatConvert.inl selects its HLSL body on `#if HLSL_VERSION > 0`.
- hlsl: the isnan() intrinsic — the bit test `(asuint(x) & 0x7fffffff) > 0x7f800000` on SM4+,
  `x != x` below, built the way isinf() is.
- hlsl: SampleGrad() gradients span the texture's own dimensions; an array slice is not a gradient
  component, so a Texture2DArray takes float2 gradients.
- hlsl: SV_Coverage as a pixel-shader INPUT: the vCoverage register, declared with a plain dcl_input
  and no interpolation mode, and kept out of the input signature like the other dedicated registers.
- hlsl: struct member functions. The lexer hands the parser each member function of a struct body as
  one METHOD_TEXT token (its full text); once the struct type exists every method is first declared,
  then defined, as the free function `__<struct>__<method>(inout <struct> __this, ...)`. Inside a
  body a bare field name reads `__this.<field>` and a bare call names a method of the same struct
  first (declared later in the struct too); `obj.Method(args)` calls it with obj as the inout
  object, and overloads resolve as for free functions.
- hlsl: `OP(k, c ? a : b)` with constants k, a, b folds into the arms, and `c ? k : k` folds to k.
  An `[unroll]` loop bounded by a select of constants then unrolls to the larger bound with
  per-iteration guards instead of running into the iteration cap.
- hlsl: the parse location is saved around an intrinsic's template compile (upstream's fix), so
  diagnostics after acos()/smoothstep()/... keep their line numbers.
- hlsl: evaluating `cond ? x : y` under each assumption of cond walks the expression graph once per
  evaluation, remembering each node's result. The graph is a DAG; walking it as a tree is exponential
  in the sharing depth, and a shader that fills a 64-entry array in one unrolled loop and indexes it
  in another never finished compiling.

Upstream vkd3d carries the location fix and none of the rest. Findings: docs/research/wine-builtin-gaps.md.
